Nicola's mother, Barbara, had first tried calling the Fuller's home at around 8.45am only to find the line engaged. The owners of the tea shop next door to the cottage recalled hearing three or four loud bangs around 9am, but they just thought it was the Fullers banging on the wall to tell them to turn their radio down. Investigators therefore deduced that the shootings had taken place sometime between 8.35am and 9am. Harry had been shot in the kitchen, his body then dragged to the nearby utility room. Given that he'd been shot in the back and there were no signs of a struggle, it was likely that he'd been targeted first. A strange white powder had been sprinkled over his torso. Next to Harry was a small plastic baggie containing the same substance.
