whoever killed them did so in cold blood. Wadhurst's High Street was a busy thoroughfare that connected the counties of East Sussex and Kant. It housed a handful of restaurants, two banks, a butcher, and several other retail stores and businesses. A high school with over a thousand students was also tucked just off the main strip, just behind Blackman's Cottage, and pupils often milled around before classes started in the morning. Yet, during the crucial time window between 8.35 and 9.00 a.m., nobody had witnessed anything particularly suspicious. Police established a command centre on High Street and set up a tip line appealing for any witnesses to come forward. An investigator told the media,
“无论谁杀了他们，都是冷血所为。”瓦德赫斯特的高街是一条繁忙的通道，连接着东萨塞克斯郡和肯特郡。这里有几家餐馆、两家银行、一家肉店以及其他几家零售店和企业。一所拥有一千多名学生的高中也坐落在主街旁，就在布莱克曼小屋后面，学生们经常在早上上课前在附近徘徊。然而，在上午 8 点 35 分到 9 点之间的关键时间窗口内，没有人目击到任何特别可疑的事情。警方在高街设立了一个指挥中心，并设立了一条举报热线，呼吁任何目击者挺身而出。一位调查人员告诉媒体：

