00:32:57.000 --> 00:33:51.000
Emergency, which service? There hadn't been any record of an emergency 999 call being placed from Blackman's Cottage. Neither police nor paramedics had been summoned to the property on the morning that Harry and Nicola were killed. Investigators now realised that Nicola might have succeeded in calling for help after all. They obtained a recording of the calls that had come through to 999 on Wednesday, February 10, 1993. At 8.34am, a call was placed from Blackman's Cottage. The caller didn't speak and only made squealing sounds down the receiver. The answering emergency services operator interpreted these sounds to be that of a child playing around and disconnected the call.
“紧急情况，什么服务？”没有任何记录显示从布莱克曼小屋拨打了 999 紧急电话。在哈里和尼古拉被杀的当天早上，警察和医护人员都没有被传唤到该房产。调查人员现在意识到尼古拉可能确实成功呼救了。他们获得了 1993 年 2 月 10 日星期三拨打 999 的电话录音。上午 8 点 34 分，从布莱克曼小屋拨出了一个电话。打电话的人没有说话，只是在听筒里发出尖叫声。接听的紧急服务接线员将这些声音解释为孩子在玩耍，并断开了通话。

38
00:33:51.000 --> 00:34:43.000
Police realised the muffled cries had actually been Nicola Fuller. The gunshot to her head that had shattered her jaw had also severed her tongue. She was trying to ask the operator for help but was unable to speak clearly. It was while she had the operator on the line that the killer placed a quilt over Nicola's head and administered the final fatal gunshot. Not knowing where the call had gone through, the killer continued walking around the house, opening and closing drawers. When Nicola's family found out about this, they were shattered. The Wadhurst police station was roughly 200 yards from Blackman's Cottage. If Nicola's call had been patched through, they believed she could have been saved,
警察意识到那些模糊的哭声实际上是尼古拉·富勒。她头部中弹，下颚碎裂，舌头也被切断了。她试图向接线员求助，但无法清晰说话。就在她与接线员通话时，凶手把被子盖在尼古拉头上，并补上了致命的一枪。不知道电话打到了哪里，凶手继续在屋里走动，开关抽屉。当尼古拉的家人发现这件事时，他们崩溃了。瓦德赫斯特警察局距离布莱克曼小屋大约 200 码。如果尼古拉的电话被转接，他们相信她本可以获救，

39
00:34:43.000 --> 00:35:41.000
or at the very least, the killer could have been caught in the act. Nicola's parents met with British Telecom, the company responsible for handling the calls, demanding an explanation and public apology. The request was denied. By April 1993, two months had passed since the double homicide and police were no closer to making an arrest. They decided it was time to reveal their full hand. A segment about the case was aired on CrimeWatch, a popular BBC television program that created reconstructions of major unsolved crimes. In it, police released an edited audio clip of Harry Fuller talking to the elusive Steve, with Steve's name cut out. A detective who worked on the case told viewers,
或者至少，凶手本可以在作案时被抓获。尼古拉的父母会见了负责处理这些电话的公司英国电信，要求解释并公开道歉。请求被拒绝。到 1993 年 4 月，双重谋杀案已经过去两个月了，警方离逮捕凶手还很远。他们决定是时候亮出底牌了。关于此案的一个片段在 BBC 的热门电视节目《犯罪观察》上播出，该节目制作了重大未决案件的重演。在节目中，警方发布了一段哈里·富勒与难以捉摸的史蒂夫交谈的剪辑音频，其中史蒂夫的名字被剪掉了。一位参与此案的侦探告诉观众：

40
00:35:41.000 --> 00:36:29.000
It's absolutely crucial that we find this man. We haven't found him, and he hasn't come forward. There may be some reason for that, but we really need to find him, and I'd ask anybody that's listening tonight who either recognises his voice, or thinks they recognise his voice, to please make contact with us. Alternatively, if the man concerned is listening and he himself wants to contact us to eliminate him, then please do contact us. A woman named Sheila was watching the segment at home. She thought she recognised the voice as her brother-in-law, Steve Young, but she couldn't be sure. Sheila decided to sleep on it.
“找到这个人绝对至关重要。我们还没有找到他，他也没有挺身而出。这可能有某种原因，但我们真的需要找到他，我会要求今晚收听的任何要么认出他的声音，要么认为自己认出他的声音的人，请与我们联系。或者，如果相关男子正在收听，并且他自己想联系我们以排除嫌疑，那么请联系我们。”一位名叫希拉的女士正在家里看这个片段。她认为她认出了那个声音是她的姐夫史蒂夫·杨，但她不能确定。希拉决定再考虑一下。

41
00:36:29.000 --> 00:37:18.000
The next day, she called Steve Young and asked if he had spoken to Harry Fuller on the night before the murders. Steve said no. Sheila was baffled. The voice had sounded so much like him. She urged her brother-in-law to contact the police anyway, just to eliminate himself from the investigation. Steve Young was Harry's insurance broker. The two had known each other since the early 80s, but had lost touch over the years. They'd only recently run into each other again and started a business relationship. About two weeks into the Fuller murder inquiry, police had questioned Steve Young as part of the routine probe into Harry's business dealings.
第二天，她打电话给史蒂夫·杨，问他是否在谋杀案发生前一天晚上与哈里·富勒交谈过。史蒂夫说没有。希拉感到困惑。那个声音听起来太像他了。她敦促她的姐夫无论如何都要联系警察，只是为了排除自己的嫌疑。史蒂夫·杨是哈里的保险经纪人。两人从 80 年代初就认识，但多年来失去了联系。他们最近才再次相遇，并开始了业务关系。在富勒谋杀案调查进行到大约两周时，警方曾作为对哈里商业交易常规调查的一部分询问过史蒂夫·杨。

42
00:37:18.000 --> 00:38:17.000
Steve said their relationship was purely professional. They didn't have a friendship outside of work. They'd last spoken about five days before the murders, when Harry called Steve to discuss a cover note that was about to expire. Steve claimed he was in his office on the morning of Wednesday, February 10, 1993, and that his secretary could verify his whereabouts. There was nothing about him that aroused police suspicions, so he wasn't looked into any further. But Sheila wasn't the only one who recognized the voice. Around the same time, an anonymous mail called the police tip line stating, The voice is Steve Young. Two days after the crime watch episode aired, two officers were dispatched to interview Steve Young at his office.
史蒂夫说他们的关系纯粹是职业性的。他们在工作之外没有友谊。他们最后一次交谈是在谋杀案发生前五天，当时哈里打电话给史蒂夫讨论一份即将到期的保险单。史蒂夫声称他在 1993 年 2 月 10 日星期三早上在办公室，他的秘书可以证明他的行踪。他身上没有任何引起警方怀疑的地方，所以他没有被进一步调查。但希拉并不是唯一一个认出那个声音的人。大约在同一时间，一名匿名邮件拨打了警方举报热线，称：“那个声音是史蒂夫·杨。”在《犯罪观察》剧集播出两天后，两名警官被派往史蒂夫·杨的办公室对他进行采访。

43
00:38:17.000 --> 00:39:09.000
Before they had the chance, they were called back. Young had just walked into the Sussex police station and identified himself as the caller on the tape. He'd also handed police a two-page statement in which he admitted that he'd initially lied to the interviewing officers. Young explained that one of his clients had a Porsche they wanted to sell. He'd told Harry Fuller about it, and he was interested in checking it out. On the evening of Tuesday, February 9, Young called Harry to arrange an inspection for 8am the following day. As Young made his way to Wadhurst the next morning, he was unexpectedly held up by roadworks. By the time he arrived at Blackman's Cottage, it was around 20 past eight.
在他们有机会之前，他们就被召回了。杨刚走进萨塞克斯警察局，并确认自己就是录音中的那个打电话的人。他还向警方递交了一份两页的声明，承认自己最初对审讯人员撒了谎。杨解释说，他的一位客户有一辆保时捷想卖。他告诉了哈里·富勒这件事，哈里很有兴趣去看看。2月9日星期二晚上，杨打电话给哈里，安排在第二天早上8点进行检查。第二天早上，当杨前往瓦德赫斯特时，意外地被道路施工耽搁了。当他到达布莱克曼小屋时，大约是8点20分。

44
00:39:09.000 --> 00:40:02.000
The curtains were drawn, so he assumed the Fullers were still asleep. Young said he knocked on the door, but there was no answer. He walked down High Street to waste some time before returning to Blackman's Cottage at around 8.40am. The curtains were still drawn, and again his knocks went unanswered. Steve Young was adamant he hadn't seen or heard anything suspicious at the property. When he found out that Harry and Nicola had been murdered, he was shocked. He claimed to have contacted the police to see if they wanted to question him, but his call was never returned, so he just assumed his statement wasn't of any interest. By the time police visited him as part of their routine questioning, he'd heard about Harry's shady business dealings.
窗帘拉着，所以他以为富勒夫妇还在睡觉。杨说他敲了门，但没有人应答。他在大街上走了一会儿，消磨时间，然后在大约早上8点40分回到布莱克曼小屋。窗帘仍然拉着，他的敲门声再次无人应答。史蒂夫·杨坚称他在那处房产没有看到或听到任何可疑的事情。当他得知哈里和尼古拉被谋杀时，他感到非常震惊。他声称曾联系警方，看他们是否想审问他，但他的电话从未得到回复，所以他只是认为他的陈述没有任何价值。当警方作为例行询问的一部分拜访他时，他已经听说了哈里那些不正当的商业交易。

45
00:40:02.000 --> 00:40:59.000
Young claimed he lied about his whereabouts on the day of the murders because he was afraid for his own safety. For investigators, there was nothing about Steve Young that raised any red flags. Aged in his mid-30s, the married father of two was a well-educated, law-abiding citizen with no criminal record. By all accounts, he was a doting husband and supportive parent. A pillar of the community, he helped to run his son's under-11 football team and was enthusiastically involved in the local drama club. Just a few months earlier, he'd stolen the show with his comedic acting skills during the village's Christmas pantomime. He was respected by the community and clients alike. Still, it was hard to comprehend why he hadn't approached the police straight away.
杨声称他在谋杀案发生当天对自己行踪撒谎是因为他担心自己的人身安全。对于调查人员来说，史蒂夫·杨身上没有任何引起怀疑的地方。这位30多岁的已婚父亲是两个孩子的父亲，是一位受过良好教育、守法的公民，没有犯罪记录。据各方说法，他是一位疼爱妻子的丈夫和支持孩子的父亲。作为社区的中坚力量，他帮助管理儿子的11岁以下足球队，并热情地参与当地的戏剧俱乐部。就在几个月前，他在村里的圣诞哑剧中以其喜剧表演技巧抢尽了风头。他受到社区和客户的尊敬。尽管如此，很难理解他为什么没有立即联系警方。

46
00:40:59.000 --> 00:42:02.000
The officer who questioned Young early on in the investigation had noted him as relaxed and normal, with nothing in his demeanour arousing any suspicion. They couldn't help but wonder if he had something to hide. Steve Young agreed to be formally interviewed. He admitted that he probably wouldn't have come forward if the recording of his call with Harry hadn't been aired on Crime Watch. Given that he hadn't seen anything that could help with the investigation, he simply didn't want to be involved in any way. When asked whether he had access to any firearms, Young said he was the treasurer of a local rifle club. He owned several guns, each of which were legally licensed, a shotgun, a revolver, and three pistols. None of them were 32-caliber pistols, the type used in the fuller murders.
在调查初期审问杨的警官指出，他表现得很放松、很正常，没有任何举止引起怀疑。他们不禁怀疑他是否有什么隐瞒。史蒂夫·杨同意接受正式审问。他承认，如果他和哈里的通话录音没有在《犯罪观察》节目中播出，他可能不会主动站出来。鉴于他没有看到任何有助于调查的事情，他只是不想以任何方式卷入其中。当被问及是否可以使用任何枪支时，杨说他是当地一家步枪俱乐部的财务主管。他拥有几支枪，每一支都有合法执照，包括一把霰弹枪、一把左轮手枪和三把手枪。它们都不是富勒谋杀案中使用的那种32口径手枪。

47
00:42:02.000 --> 00:42:56.000
Even though they had no evidence to link him to the crime, police suspected Steve Young knew more than he was letting on. They placed him under arrest while further investigation was conducted, treading carefully with Young in a bid to keep him talking. Police looked in to Steve Young's movements on Wednesday, February 10. After leaving Blackman's Cottage, it was a typical working day for the insurance broker. He had some meetings, spoke with some business associates, and chatted on the phone with his wife. In the evening, he attended a meeting at the Freemasons Lodge, where he was a member. He'd been his normal self. Nobody had noticed anything strange about his behaviour. A warrant was obtained to search Young's home and office.
尽管没有任何证据将他与犯罪联系起来，但警方怀疑史蒂夫·杨知道的比他透露的要多。他们在进行进一步调查时将他逮捕，并小心翼翼地对待杨，试图让他继续开口。警方调查了史蒂夫·杨在2月10日星期三的行踪。离开布莱克曼小屋后，对于这位保险经纪人来说，这是典型的工作日。他开了一些会，与一些商业伙伴交谈，并与妻子通了电话。晚上，他参加了共济会分会的一次会议，他是那里的成员。他表现得和平常一样。没有人注意到他的行为有什么奇怪之处。警方获得了搜查杨家和办公室的搜查令。

48
00:42:56.000 --> 00:44:04.000
While he'd already admitted to being a gun enthusiast who was legally licensed to own multiple weapons, police were shocked at what they found. In addition to the firearms Young had already disclosed, they found deactivated grenade launchers, bayonets, replica submachine guns, combat gear, masks, and even fake number plates. One of the illegal guns, a loaded 9mm automatic pistol, had been stashed underneath the bed of one of Young's children. The search also uncovered thousands of rounds of ammunition. When the collection of arsenal was laid out, it filled the size of a squash cord. While this was deeply troubling, one weapon was notably absent, a .32 caliber pistol. Young had already told police that he topped up his ammunition supply by reloading. This is a common practice used by gun enthusiasts to save money.
虽然他已经承认自己是一名枪支爱好者，并合法拥有多件武器，但警方对他所发现的东西感到震惊。除了杨已经披露的枪支外，他们还发现了已失效的榴弹发射器、刺刀、仿制冲锋枪、作战装备、面具，甚至还有假车牌。其中一把非法枪支，一把装满子弹的9毫米自动手枪，被藏在杨的一个孩子床下。搜查还发现了数千发弹药。当这些军火被摆出来时，填满了壁球场那么大的空间。虽然这非常令人不安，但有一件武器明显缺失，那就是一把32口径的手枪。杨此前曾告诉警方，他通过重新装填来补充弹药供应。这是枪支爱好者为了省钱而常用的做法。

49
00:44:04.000 --> 00:44:53.000
Instead of purchasing mass-produced ammunition, one can collect empty cases and then assemble the individual components, including gunpowder, primers, and bullet heads. Police found Young's reloading machine. The markings on his reloaded ammunition was compared to the ammunition recovered from Blackman's cottage. They looked remarkably similar. When the police asked Young what car he drove to Blackman's cottage, he was oddly cagey. He ummed and arred before saying it was probably his white Volkswagen Golf. The police looked for the car at Young's home and office. It wasn't there.
与其购买批量生产的弹药，不如收集空弹壳，然后组装各个部件，包括火药、底火和弹头。警方发现了杨的复装机。他复装弹药上的标记与从布莱克曼小屋回收的弹药进行了比对。它们看起来非常相似。当警方问杨他开车去布莱克曼小屋时开的是什么车时，他表现得异常闪烁其词。他支支吾吾，然后说可能是他的白色大众高尔夫。警方在杨的家和办公室寻找这辆车。它不在那里。

50
00:44:53.000 --> 00:46:00.000
They asked him where it was, and he said he'd recently taken it to a mechanic to have some work done. Police tracked the Golf down, only to discover that Young had only taken it in the day after the segment about the Fuller's murders had aired on CrimeWatch. A mobile telephone inside the vehicle was confirmed to have made a call to the Fuller's home at 8.10 on the morning of the murders. Although the Volkswagen Golf was a popular model, Young's vehicle was unique looking with distinct modifications, including alloy wheels. This made it easy for investigators to differentiate it from other white cars when reviewing the security footage taken from Lloyd's bank. They focused on the times that Steve Young claimed to have arrived and departed from the area, 8.20 and 8.40 am. But there was no sign of the Golf. They viewed the footage captured earlier and later than the times Young had given.
他们问他车在哪里，他说他最近把它送到修理厂去维修了。警方追踪到了那辆高尔夫，却发现杨是在《犯罪观察》播出关于富勒谋杀案的片段后的第二天，才把它送去修理的。车内的一部移动电话被证实曾在谋杀案当天早上8点10分拨打过富勒家。虽然大众高尔夫是一款流行的车型，但杨的车辆外观独特，有明显的改装，包括合金轮毂。这使得调查人员在查看劳埃德银行的监控录像时，很容易将其与其他白色汽车区分开来。他们重点关注了史蒂夫·杨声称到达和离开该地区的时间，即早上8点20分和8点40分。但没有高尔夫的踪影。他们查看了杨提供的时间之前和之后的录像。

51
00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:44.000
Sure enough, they found the car. He'd been caught in yet another lie. With the circumstantial evidence mounting against Steve Young, the biggest question was, why would he want to kill Harry and Nicola Fuller? He had no known grudges with either of them, nor was there anything to suggest any kind of romantic involvement. In fact, he barely knew them. Police asked Young about his financial situation. He responded it was pretty tight. This soon proved to be a major understatement.
果然，他们找到了那辆车。他又一次撒谎被抓住了。随着针对史蒂夫·杨的间接证据越来越多，最大的问题是，他为什么要杀害哈里和尼古拉·富勒？他与他们两人之间没有已知的恩怨，也没有任何迹象表明有任何形式的浪漫关系。事实上，他几乎不认识他们。警方询问了杨的财务状况。他回答说非常紧张。这很快被证明是一个严重的轻描淡写。

52
00:46:44.000 --> 00:47:37.000
Steve Young was deep in debt. He'd inherited his home from his father, but had since taken out several mortgages, which had overdue payments. His insurance brokerage was trading insolvently and hadn't turned a profit in 8 years. Instead of using his client's money to pay their insurance premiums, Young was using it to pay off his own debts. With no funds left over to pay the insurance companies, his brokerage was under threat of being shut down. His financial situation was deemed critical. All up, Young owed over £100,000 to multiple friends, family members and businesses. The provincial insurance company was one such business.
史蒂夫·杨债台高筑。他从父亲那里继承了房子，但此后又申请了几笔抵押贷款，这些贷款都有逾期还款。他的保险经纪公司经营不善，已经8年没有盈利了。杨没有用客户的钱支付他们的保险费，而是用它来偿还自己的债务。由于没有剩余资金支付给保险公司，他的经纪公司面临倒闭的威胁。他的财务状况被认为是危急的。总而言之，杨欠多位朋友、家人和企业超过10万英镑。省保险公司就是其中之一。

53
00:47:37.000 --> 00:48:27.000
Young owed them £13,500 in back-dated premiums. Police discovered that just two days before Harry and Nicola were killed, a representative from provincial had called Young. He said he'd be coming to Young's office on Wednesday, February 10 to collect the outstanding debt. If he didn't pay up, they'd no longer do business with him. The appointment went ahead as planned. Young handed over a check for £6,000, which cleared with no problems. Police discovered that Young kept a detailed record of all the people he borrowed money from. There was no record of him having borrowed a large sum of money before this meeting.
杨欠他们13500英镑的过期保费。警方发现，就在哈里和尼古拉被杀的前两天，省保险公司的一名代表曾给杨打过电话。他说他将于2月10日星期三来到杨的办公室收取欠款。如果他不付钱，他们将不再与他做生意。预约按计划进行。杨交出了一张6000英镑的支票，支票顺利兑现了。警方发现，杨详细记录了他借钱的所有人。在这次会议之前，没有他借过大笔钱的记录。

54
00:48:27.000 --> 00:49:33.000
This raised the obvious question. Where did he get his money from? A check of Steve Young's bank records confirmed that he'd deposited £6,000 into his business account on the morning of Wednesday, February 10, just after Harry and Nicola were killed. The deposit was made in £20 notes, just like the unaccounted for payment that Harry Fuller had received from his neighbour. Young had also paid off an outstanding phone bill of £360. The police asked Young where he got this cash from. He explained that a friend had lent it to him two years ago and he'd been hanging onto it in case of an emergency. Meanwhile, an officer searching Young's office found a single 32-caliber Hertenberger bullet. A ballistics expert examined it and determined it had been shot from a Walther PPK self-loading pistol.
这引出了一个显而易见的问题。他的钱是从哪里来的？对史蒂夫·杨银行记录的核查证实，他在2月10日星期三早上，也就是哈里和尼古拉被杀后不久，向他的商业账户存入了6000英镑。这笔存款是用20英镑面值的钞票存入的，就像哈里·富勒从邻居那里收到的那笔无法解释的款项一样。杨还偿还了360英镑的逾期电话费。警方问杨这些现金是从哪里来的。他解释说，一位朋友两年前借给他的，他一直留着以备不时之需。与此同时，一名搜查杨办公室的警官发现了一颗32口径的赫滕伯格子弹。弹道专家检查后确定它是从瓦尔特PPK自装手枪中射出的。

55
00:49:33.000 --> 00:50:57.000
The same as the gun used to kill Harry and Nicola Fuller. Case file will be back shortly. Thank you for supporting us by listening to this episode's sponsors. Thank you for listening to this episode's ads. By supporting our sponsors, you support Case File to continue to deliver quality content. When pressed, Young maintained his innocence. He explained that he'd once reloaded some 32-caliber ammunition for another member of his gun club but had never owned such a weapon himself. It was no use. He'd been caught in too many lies. Steve Young was formally charged with the double murder of Harry and Nicola Fuller. Police dubbed him the Ice Man for the way he was able to go about his life immediately after the crimes as though nothing had happened.
与杀死哈里和尼古拉·富勒的枪相同。案件档案很快就会回来。感谢您通过收听本集赞助商来支持我们。感谢您收听本集的广告。通过支持我们的赞助商，您支持Case File继续提供高质量的内容。当被追问时，杨坚称自己是无辜的。他解释说，他曾经为枪支俱乐部的另一名成员复装过一些32口径的弹药，但自己从未拥有过这样的武器。没用了。他撒了太多的谎。史蒂夫·杨被正式指控犯有哈里和尼古拉·富勒的双重谋杀罪。警方称他为“冰人”，因为他在犯罪后能够立即像什么都没发生一样继续他的生活。

