00:50:57.000 --> 00:51:46.000
Harry and Nicola's families were stunned. Young lived just down the road from Harry's brother, Tom, and they sometimes ran into each other at the local pub. He couldn't believe that such an apparently normal person could commit such a heinous crime. To Nicola's family, Young was a complete stranger. Her sister Michelle told Crime Watch, I found it hard to believe that their insurance broker would have access to guns, let alone that he would commit such a crime. It didn't seem to fit the character or the sort of person you assume an assurance broker to be. But then, what is a murderer like? What job do they do?
哈里和尼古拉的家人惊呆了。杨就住在哈里的兄弟汤姆家附近，他们有时会在当地的酒吧碰面。他无法相信一个看起来如此正常的人竟然能犯下如此令人发指的罪行。对于尼古拉的家人来说，杨是一个完全的陌生人。她的妹妹米歇尔告诉《犯罪观察》：“我很难相信他们的保险经纪人会接触到枪支，更不用说他会犯下这样的罪行。这似乎不符合性格，也不符合你认为保险经纪人应该是的那种人。但话说回来，杀人犯是什么样的？他们做什么工作？”

57
00:51:46.000 --> 00:52:55.000
In the first week of May, three months after they were killed, Harry and Nicola were laid to rest in separate ceremonies. Their funerals suited their personalities. Harry's a large event and Nicola's modest and private. Nicola's funeral took place the day after Harry's at the same church where the pair's marriage had been blessed just eight months prior. The presiding reverend told the Kent and Sussex courier, You cannot make sense of a nonsense like this. It is hard to do anything other than stand together in sorrow and sadness. Steve Young's trial for the double murder commenced in late February 1994 and just over a year after Harry and Nicola were killed. The prosecution's case was relatively straightforward. While the evidence against Young was circumstantial, they said his dire financial situation gave him motivation to target Harry Fuller, who was known to carry large sums of cash.
5月的第一周，在他们被杀三个月后，哈里和尼古拉在单独的仪式上入土为安。他们的葬礼符合他们的个性。哈里的葬礼规模宏大，尼古拉的则朴素而私密。尼古拉的葬礼在哈里的葬礼后一天举行，地点就在八个月前这对夫妇举行婚礼祝福的同一座教堂。主持的牧师告诉《肯特和萨塞克斯信使报》：“你无法理解这样的荒唐事。除了在悲伤和哀痛中站在一起，很难做任何其他事情。”史蒂夫·杨的双重谋杀案审判于1994年2月下旬开始，距离哈里和尼古拉被杀仅一年多一点。检方的案子相对简单。虽然针对杨的证据是间接的，但他们表示，他糟糕的财务状况给了他针对哈里·富勒的动机，因为哈里以携带大量现金而闻名。

58
00:52:55.000 --> 00:53:56.000
By setting up a meeting with Harry about his client's Porsche, he established an explanation for his presence at Blackman's Cottage. His access to firearms gave him the means to carry out the crime, while the discovery of similar bullets to those used in the murders proved a link. His changing stories and the lies he told to police were further proof of his guilt. Nicola Fuller was a victim of collateral damage. Young had shot her purely to avoid her identifying him as her husband's killer. The defense disputed this entirely. If Young's sole motive was financial gain, there were plenty of other people who could have targeted Harry Fuller for this same reason. What about his other enemies and scorned business associates? And if all Young wanted was a quick cash grab, why not break in and rob Blackman's Cottage when nobody was home?
通过安排与哈里会面讨论他客户的保时捷，他为自己出现在布莱克曼小屋找到了解释。他接触枪支的途径给了他实施犯罪的手段，而发现与谋杀案中使用的子弹相似的子弹证明了联系。他不断变化的说法和对警方撒的谎是他有罪的进一步证明。尼古拉·富勒是附带损害的受害者。杨射杀她纯粹是为了避免她认出他是她丈夫的杀手。辩方完全反驳了这一点。如果杨唯一的动机是经济利益，那么还有很多人可以因为同样的原因针对哈里·富勒。他其他的敌人和被轻视的商业伙伴呢？如果杨想要的只是快速抢钱，为什么不在没人时闯入并抢劫布莱克曼小屋呢？

59
00:53:56.000 --> 00:55:03.000
If Nicola wasn't a target, why didn't he organise to meet Harry at a different location or when he was alone? The courtroom was tense as Steve Young took the stand in his own defense. In an unexpected twist, he provided a brand new account of the events that unfolded on the morning of February 10. For the first time, Young gave an explanation for the 8.10am phone call between himself and Harry Fuller. He claimed that he called Harry upon his arrival to Blackman's Cottage because the curtains were all drawn and there was no response when he knocked on the door. The call apparently woke Harry up. Harry told Young to give him some time, so Young waited in his car. A short while later, he noticed that a curtain had been opened. He knocked again but still there was no response. He walked to the rear of the property in case Harry had decided to wait for him in the car park.
如果尼古拉不是目标，为什么他不安排在不同的地点或在他独自一人时与哈里会面？当史蒂夫·杨为自己的辩护出庭作证时，法庭气氛紧张。在一个意想不到的转折中，他提供了关于2月10日早上发生事件的全新叙述。杨第一次解释了自己和哈里·富勒之间早上8点10分的电话。他声称，他在到达布莱克曼小屋时给哈里打了电话，因为窗帘都拉着，他敲门时没有人回应。这个电话显然把哈里吵醒了。哈里告诉杨给他一点时间，所以杨在车里等。过了一会儿，他注意到窗帘被拉开了。他又敲了一次门，但仍然没有人回应。他走到房产后面，以防哈里决定在停车场等他。

60
00:55:03.000 --> 00:55:56.000
When he got there, he saw that the back door was slightly open. Young looked inside and saw Harry lying on the ground. He rushed inside and felt for a pulse, but there wasn't one. At first, he assumed Harry had a heart attack, but he then noticed blood was coming from Harry's head. A cartridge case was lying nearby. From his experience with guns, Young said he recognized it as being from a 32 calibre bullet. For the first time, Young admitted that he had once owned a replica .32 Walther PPK pistol. He said he'd purchased it from a Chinese mail order five years prior, but had since sold it to someone else – Harry Fuller.
当他到达那里时，他看到后门微微敞开。杨往里看，看到哈里躺在地上。他冲进去摸了摸脉搏，但没有脉搏。起初，他以为哈里心脏病发作了，但他随后注意到哈里的头部在流血。附近躺着一个弹壳。根据他的枪支经验，杨说他认出那是32口径子弹的弹壳。杨第一次承认他曾经拥有一把仿制.32瓦尔特PPK手枪。他说他是五年前从一家中国邮购公司购买的，但后来把它卖给了别人——哈里·富勒。

61
00:55:56.000 --> 00:56:54.000
Young claimed that in the months before Harry was killed, he and another man approached Young at his office, asking if he could help Harry purchase a gun for protection. Young sold him the Walther PPK, along with some of his reloaded ammunition. Young said that upon realizing Harry was dead, he panicked. He immediately fled outside. Looking back at the house, he saw an unfamiliar face of a boarding male in the upstairs window. Young dialed 999, but then paused. Harry Fuller had been killed by the very weapon that Young had sold him illegally. Fearing that he'd be incorrectly linked to the crime or that his life would be in danger for being a witness, he made the difficult decision to keep what he saw to himself.
杨声称，在哈里被杀前的几个月里，他和另一个男人在办公室找到杨，问他是否能帮助哈里购买一把枪用于自卫。杨把瓦尔特PPK卖给了他，还有一些他复装的弹药。杨说，当意识到哈里死了，他惊慌失措。他立即逃到外面。回头看房子时，他看到楼上的窗户里有一个陌生的男人的脸。杨拨打了999，但随后停顿了。哈里·富勒是被杨非法卖给他的武器杀死的。由于担心自己会被错误地与犯罪联系起来，或者因为作为目击者而生命受到威胁，他做出了一个艰难的决定，将他所看到的一切保密。

62
00:56:54.000 --> 00:57:51.000
In the weeks following, Young said that an anonymous male called his office multiple times making threats against him and his family. His fear was so immense that he was compelled to lie and put on a façade of calm when questioned by the police. The defence presented the possibility that another of Harry's enemies had entered Blackman's cottage that morning. Perhaps Harry had drawn his gun on the assailant, who managed to take hold of the weapon themselves, and then used it to kill the couple. The prosecution disputed this. Had someone gone to the Fuller's home with the intention to kill, common sense dictated that they would have brought their own weapon. Also, Harry had been shot from behind at close range. It was unlikely he would have turned his back while a gun was being aimed at him.
在接下来的几周里，杨说一个匿名男子多次给他的办公室打电话，威胁他和他的家人。他的恐惧如此强烈，以至于他在接受警方询问时被迫撒谎并装出一副冷静的样子。辩方提出了哈里的另一个敌人那天早上进入布莱克曼小屋的可能性。也许哈里对袭击者拔出了枪，袭击者设法夺取了武器，然后用它杀死了这对夫妇。检方反驳了这一点。如果有人带着杀人的意图去富勒家，常识告诉他们会带上自己的武器。此外，哈里是从背后近距离被射杀的。他不太可能在有人瞄准他时背对着对方。

63
00:57:51.000 --> 00:58:58.000
Young's story about selling Harry his Walther PPK along with some of his reloaded ammunition also seemed suspiciously convenient. He'd only mentioned this after becoming aware of the fact that 32 caliber ammo had been uncovered in his office. After four weeks of testimony, the jury deliberated overnight before delivering its verdict. For the murders of Harry and Nicola Fuller, Steve Young was found guilty and given two life sentences. A motion in the courtroom was mixed. Some of the victim's loved ones cheered while Young's wife broke down in tears. Although Nicola's family were relieved, her father told reporters, the verdict doesn't change things for us at all. We can't bring Nicci back, but this does take an evil person off the streets. Harry and Nicola's loved ones could finally begin the healing process.
杨关于卖给哈里瓦尔特PPK以及一些复装弹药的故事看起来也极其巧合。他只有在意识到他的办公室里发现了32口径弹药后才提到这一点。经过四周的证词，陪审团彻夜商议后作出了裁决。对于哈里和尼古拉·富勒的谋杀案，史蒂夫·杨被判有罪，并被判处两次终身监禁。法庭上的反应不一。一些受害者的亲人欢呼雀跃，而杨的妻子则泪流满面。虽然尼古拉的家人感到宽慰，但她的父亲告诉记者：“判决对我们来说根本没有改变任何事情。我们无法让尼基回来，但这确实把一个邪恶的人从街上带走了。”哈里和尼古拉的亲人终于可以开始愈合过程了。

64
00:58:58.000 --> 00:59:59.000
But for one member of the jury, the nightmare was just beginning. For weeks after the trial, 24 year old juror Adrian lay awake at night, plagued with a secret. Something had happened during the trial that didn't sit well with him. He was torn. Did he keep it to himself, or did others have the right to know the truth? Adrian deliberated internally before eventually seeking legal advice. Most solicitors didn't want to get involved, likely because it was illegal to repeat anything that jurors told them. But as the weeks went by, Adrian could no longer live with the knowledge of what had happened behind closed doors. The night before Steve Young's verdict was delivered, the 12 member jury had been sequestered to a hotel to deliberate.
但对于陪审团的一名成员来说，噩梦才刚刚开始。审判后的几周里，24岁的陪审员阿德里安晚上躺在床上睡不着觉，被一个秘密所困扰。审判期间发生了一些让他感到不安的事情。他很纠结。他是应该把它藏在心里，还是其他人有权知道真相？阿德里安在内心挣扎后，最终寻求了法律建议。大多数律师不想卷入其中，很可能是因为重复陪审员告诉他们的任何事情都是违法的。但随着几周过去，阿德里安再也无法忍受闭门造车所发生的事情的真相。在史蒂夫·杨的判决宣布的前一天晚上，12名陪审员被隔离在一家酒店进行商议。

65
00:59:59.000 --> 01:00:53.000
This is standard practice in many countries. It ensures that jurors have minimal access to the outside world, thus preventing exposure to external influences or information while they reach a decision. It had been a long four weeks for the jurors. Not only were they conflicted as to whether or not Steve Young was telling the truth, they'd also had to sit through the six minute recording of Nicola Fuller's thwarted attempt to call for help. It took an emotional toll. Once the jurors were in the hotel, they sat down over dinner and had a few drinks to try and unwind. The atmosphere quickly became more relaxed. People joked around and engaged in casual conversation, lifting the mood considerably.
这是许多国家的标准做法。它确保陪审员与外界的接触最少，从而防止在达成决定时接触到外部影响或信息。对于陪审员来说，这是漫长的四周。他们不仅在史蒂夫·杨是否说真话的问题上存在分歧，还不得不坐着听完尼古拉·富勒试图呼救的六分钟录音。这造成了情感上的伤害。陪审员们进入酒店后，坐下来吃晚饭，喝了几杯酒，试图放松一下。气氛很快变得更加轻松。人们开玩笑，进行随意的交谈，气氛大为好转。

66
01:00:53.000 --> 01:02:04.000
An entertaining conversation arose about seances and who among them had participated in one before. A seance is a meeting in which people attempt to communicate with the spirit world. While the concept of contacting the dead has been around for centuries, it wasn't until the late 1800s that the very first device was sold to facilitate communication between the living and deceased. Known as a Ouija board, the device consists of a flat board displaying all the letters of the alphabet, the numbers zero through nine, and the words yes, no, and goodbye. At the bottom is a small heart-shaped plank known as the planchette. To use a Ouija board, two or more people gather round the board, gently placing their hands on the planchette. They then ask questions and watch as the planchette moves around the board, spilling out messages from the other side. The Ouija board is a controversial device.
一个关于降神会以及他们中谁以前参加过降神会的有趣谈话出现了。降神会是人们试图与灵界交流的会议。虽然接触死者的概念已经存在了几个世纪，但直到19世纪末，第一台促进生者与死者之间交流的设备才被出售。这种设备被称为通灵板，由一块平坦的板子组成，上面显示了所有字母表、数字0到9以及“是”、“否”和“再见”等词。底部是一块心形的小木板，称为指针。要使用通灵板，两个或更多人围在板子周围，轻轻地将手放在指针上。然后他们提出问题，看着指针在板子上移动，拼出来自另一边的信息。通灵板是一种有争议的设备。

67
01:02:04.000 --> 01:03:18.000
Some view it as a valuable means to communicate with the spirit world, while others believe it's a satanic tool that can open menacing portals into the unknown. Scientists believe the so-called messages received on a Ouija board are simply the result of the user's subconscious. To skeptics, the planchette isn't moved across the board by a spiritual being, but by the users themselves. Whatever the truth, most people tend to agree on one thing. Ouija boards are not to be messed with. The group of jurors laughed and shared stories about their experience with seances before retiring to their rooms for the 11pm curfew. Adrienne was feeling quite tipsy and went straight to bed. But a small group, one man and three women, weren't ready to call it a night. Intrigued by the conversation about seances, they gathered in one of their hotel rooms and decided to hold one of their own. They fashioned their very own Ouija board out of paper using a wine glass as the planchette.
有些人认为它是与灵界交流的宝贵手段，而另一些人则认为它是可以打开通往未知世界的威胁性门户的撒旦工具。科学家认为，在通灵板上收到的所谓信息仅仅是用户潜意识的结果。对于怀疑论者来说，指针不是由灵体在板子上移动的，而是由用户自己移动的。无论真相如何，大多数人倾向于同意一件事。通灵板是不能乱玩的。这群陪审员笑着分享了他们参加降神会的经历，然后回到房间遵守晚上11点的宵禁。阿德里安喝得有点醉，直接上床睡觉了。但一小群人，一名男子和三名女子，还没准备好结束这一夜。被关于降神会的谈话所吸引，他们聚集在其中一个酒店房间里，决定自己举行一次。他们用纸制作了自己的通灵板，用酒杯作为指针。

68
01:03:18.000 --> 01:04:04.000
The foursome then sat around the board, each of them placing their fingers on the base of the glass. They asked if there were any spirits present. The answer was yes. The group asked the spirit to identify themselves. The planchette moved across the board from letter to letter, finally spelling out the name Harry Fuller. The group grew tense. The designated leader asked, who killed you? They watched in silence as the wine glass slid across the board, eventually spelling out the words, Stephen Young did it.
四个人围坐在板子周围，每个人都把手指放在杯底。他们问是否有任何灵体在场。答案是肯定的。小组要求灵体表明身份。指针在板子上从一个字母移动到另一个字母，最后拼出了“哈里·富勒”的名字。小组变得紧张起来。指定的领导者问：“是谁杀了你？”他们静静地看着酒杯在板子上滑动，最终拼出了“史蒂夫·杨干的”这些字。

69
01:04:04.000 --> 01:04:51.000
The leader asked what they should do. The response, vote guilty tomorrow. For some of the women, it became too much. They started to cry, thinking they'd taken things way too far. The seance ended and the group retreated to their respective rooms, tormented by what they'd done. The next morning, Adrian heard them discussing it over breakfast. He couldn't believe they'd actually gone through with it. At first, he thought it was funny. But, when Steve Young was declared guilty later that day, Adrian wondered whether a miscarriage of justice had been served.
领导者问他们该怎么办。回答是：“明天投有罪票。”对于一些女性来说，这太过分了。她们开始哭泣，认为自己把事情做得太过火了。降神会结束了，小组成员退回到各自的房间，被他们所做的事情折磨着。第二天早上，阿德里安听到他们在早餐时讨论这件事。他无法相信他们真的这么做了。起初，他觉得这很有趣。但是，当史蒂夫·杨当天晚些时候被宣布有罪时，阿德里安怀疑是否发生了司法不公。

70
01:04:51.000 --> 01:05:49.000
Four weeks after the trial, Adrian couldn't live with the knowledge anymore. He wrote an anonymous letter to the Crown Court, detailing the antics at the hotel and requesting that Steve Young's conviction be quashed. Shortly after, he approached the News of the World tabloid and gave them the full exclusive story, saying, This is someone's life we're dealing with. I was astonished that these grown-up people had played this child's game. News of the World published the story under the headline, Boo's Dirty Jokes and the Ouija Board. It quickly became a media sensation. A jury is expected to reach a verdict based on the facts presented at trial, not on potentially unreliable external information.
审判结束四周后，阿德里安再也无法忍受这个秘密了。他给刑事法庭写了一封匿名信，详细描述了酒店里的闹剧，并要求撤销史蒂夫·杨的定罪。不久之后，他联系了《世界新闻报》小报，并给了他们完整的独家报道，说：“这是我们正在处理的某人的生命。我感到震惊的是，这些成年人竟然玩了这个孩子的游戏。”《世界新闻报》以“嘘声、脏笑话和通灵板”为标题发表了这篇报道。它很快成为媒体轰动事件。陪审团应根据审判中提出的事实达成裁决，而不是根据可能不可靠的外部信息。

