01:05:49.000 --> 01:07:03.000
Being swayed by external influence or attempting to acquire further evidence was potentially a criminal offence. Adrian's allegations were therefore treated with utmost seriousness. A full investigation was launched to determine whether those who held the seance had attempted to pervert the course of justice. The four jury members insisted that the decision to use the Ouija Board had been nothing more than a poor decision fueled by alcohol. Despite some of their emotional reactions, they each viewed the whole thing as a joke and were adamant that the answers given by the so-called spirit had nothing to do with their decision to convict Steve Young. It took six months of questioning and deliberations before the court declared that while the jury had misbehaved, nothing criminal had occurred. Steve Young's legal team appealed his conviction based in part on the jury's misbehavior and the court agreed. A retrial was ordered. The court's opinion provoked some fascinating discussions for the legal community.
受到外部影响或试图获取进一步证据可能是一种刑事犯罪。因此，阿德里安的指控受到了极其严肃的对待。一项全面的调查启动，以确定那些举行降神会的人是否试图妨碍司法公正。四名陪审员坚持认为，使用通灵板的决定只不过是一个受酒精影响的糟糕决定。尽管他们中的一些人有情绪反应，但他们每个人都把整件事看作是一个玩笑，并坚称所谓灵体给出的答案与他们定罪史蒂夫·杨的决定无关。经过六个月的询问和商议，法院宣布，虽然陪审团行为不端，但没有发生任何犯罪行为。史蒂夫·杨的法律团队部分基于陪审团的不当行为对他的定罪提出上诉，法院同意了。法院下令重审。法院的意见在法律界引发了一些引人入胜的讨论。

72
01:07:03.000 --> 01:08:30.000
Law professor Gary Slapper discussed the issue in the Times newspaper, saying, Suppose the jurors in the hotel had sought advice from their God through prayer. Would such a course of action invalidate their decision? They would, after all, be consulting something non-corporeal and something other than the evidence in the case. The divine and superstitious oracles both rely on the faith of the juror. Will the court of appeal be able to argue that consulting a God for guidance is permissible, but that consulting any other non-corporeal entity is not allowed? Harry and Nicholas' families were eager to put the trauma of the trial behind them and move on with their lives. When they heard that Young's conviction was overturned, they were gutted. Harry's family couldn't believe that a man proven guilty in court could get a retrial on what they viewed as such a, quote, silly, silly thing. Nicholas' family didn't think they could get through it a second time around. They were furious that the media had latched onto the sensational Ouija board story, saying that the jurors had made a complete mockery of their daughter's death.
法学教授加里·斯拉珀在《泰晤士报》上讨论了这个问题，他说：“假设酒店里的陪审员通过祈祷寻求上帝的建议。这样的行动会使他们的决定无效吗？毕竟，他们会咨询非物质的东西，而不是案件中的证据。神圣和迷信的预言都依赖于陪审员的信仰。上诉法院能否辩称，咨询上帝寻求指导是允许的，但咨询任何其他非物质实体是不允许的？”哈里和尼古拉的家人渴望将审判的创伤抛在脑后，继续他们的生活。当他们听说杨的定罪被推翻时，他们感到非常痛苦。哈里的家人无法相信一个在法庭上被证明有罪的人，竟然能因为他们认为如此“愚蠢、愚蠢的事情”而获得重审。尼古拉的家人认为他们无法第二次经历这一切。他们对媒体抓住耸人听闻的通灵板故事感到愤怒，称陪审员完全嘲弄了他们女儿的死。

73
01:08:30.000 --> 01:09:25.000
The retrial of Steve Young for the murders of Harry and Nicholas Fuller went ahead eight months later in front of a brand new jury. For three weeks, Harry and Nicholas loved ones had to endure the harrowing evidence for a second time. But once again, the jury unanimously found Steve Young guilty for both murders. The judge called him a cold-blooded killer who had committed the crimes for his own personal gain before serving him with two life sentences. When asked if he had anything to say, Young simply stated, I'm innocent, my lord. Outside court, Harry's brother Tom told reporters, Steven Young is an animal who should be put down. I would like to see hanging brought back for people like him.
史蒂夫·杨因谋杀哈里和尼古拉·富勒的重审在八个月后在全新的陪审团面前进行。三周来，哈里和尼古拉的亲人不得不第二次忍受令人痛苦的证据。但陪审团再次一致裁定史蒂夫·杨两项谋杀罪名成立。法官称他为冷血杀手，为了个人利益犯下了这些罪行，随后判处他两次终身监禁。当被问及有什么话要说时，杨只是简单地说：“法官大人，我是无辜的。”法庭外，哈里的兄弟汤姆告诉记者：“史蒂夫·杨是一个应该被处死的畜生。我希望看到像他这样的人被恢复绞刑。”

74
01:09:25.000 --> 01:10:55.000
You can hardly explain what it has been like for both families to go through this ordeal. It's like someone having their hand in your guts and slowly pulling them out. Some struggled to comprehend that an upstanding family man like Steve Young could be compelled to commit such a callous crime, no matter his motivation. Theories remained that he wasn't the only one at the Fuller's house on February 10, 1993. There was still the matter of the witnesses who had reported seeing two mysterious men approaching Blackman's Cottage on the morning of the murders. Although these sightings were never confirmed, it fueled ongoing speculation that Steve Young could have been working with one of Harry Fuller's enemies, either by force or out of financial desperation. Given Young's access to firearms, his clean criminal record, and his rapport with Harry, Young arguably made a desirable partner for someone who wanted to cause more harm to Harry than simply taking his money. It was even theorized that Young could have agreed to help set up the meeting, not knowing what was about to transpire. But no evidence was ever uncovered to support this, and no one else was ever charged in relation to the crime.
你很难解释两个家庭经历这种磨难是什么感觉。就像有人把手伸进你的内脏里慢慢地把它们拉出来一样。一些人难以理解像史蒂夫·杨这样受人尊敬的顾家男人，无论动机如何，怎么会被迫犯下如此冷酷的罪行。理论仍然认为，1993年2月10日，他并不是唯一一个在富勒家的人。还有目击者报告说，在谋杀案当天早上看到两名神秘男子接近布莱克曼小屋。虽然这些目击事件从未得到证实，但这助长了持续的猜测，即史蒂夫·杨可能与哈里·富勒的敌人之一合作，无论是被迫还是出于经济绝望。鉴于杨接触枪支的途径、他干净的犯罪记录以及他与哈里的融洽关系，对于那些想对哈里造成比仅仅拿走他的钱更大的伤害的人来说，杨可以说是一个理想的伙伴。甚至有人推测，杨可能同意帮助安排会面，却不知道接下来会发生什么。但从未发现任何证据支持这一点，也没有其他人因该罪行被起诉。

75
01:10:55.000 --> 01:12:07.000
The trial of Steve Young has made history as one of the high-profile examples of juror misbehavior. Decades later, the behavior of the jurors is still questioned. Harry Fuller's brother Tom felt the original jurors should be punished for what they did, saying, We all went through months more agony because of them. Detective Graham Hill, who worked on the Fuller murder investigation, told the ABC, This is making an absolute mockery, and it's the most serious type of trial you can ever have. There is no element of humour in it at all, there's no frivolity in it at all, and yet those four members of the jury made it into a laughing stock. University of Melbourne law professor Jeremy Gans wrote a book centered around the case, titled The Ouija Board Jurors, Mystery, Mischief and Misery in the Jury System. In it, he explores other cases of jury misconduct, concluding that there was nothing exceptional about the Ouija Board jurors other than the tabloid media attention.
史蒂夫·杨的审判作为陪审员不当行为的高调案例之一载入史册。几十年后，陪审员的行为仍然受到质疑。哈里·富勒的兄弟汤姆认为最初的陪审员应该因为他们的所作所为而受到惩罚，他说：“因为他们，我们所有人都经历了几个月的痛苦。”参与富勒谋杀案调查的侦探格雷厄姆·希尔告诉澳大利亚广播公司：“这简直是在嘲弄，这是你所能经历的最严重的审判。它没有任何幽默成分，没有任何轻浮成分，然而那四名陪审员却把它变成了一个笑柄。”墨尔本大学法学教授杰里米·甘斯写了一本以该案为中心的书，题为《通灵板陪审员：陪审团制度中的神秘、恶作剧和苦难》。在书中，他探讨了其他陪审团不当行为的案例，得出的结论是，除了小报媒体的关注外，通灵板陪审员没有什么特别之处。

76
01:12:07.000 --> 01:13:15.000
Gans disputes the general perception that the jurors were making a mockery of the Fuller case and treating the hotel sequestering as a party. Instead, he points out that they had to sit through disturbing evidence, including the failed 999 call from Nicola, which would have been incredibly traumatic. Professor Gans told the ABC, Whatever was going on in that hotel room probably wasn't good times for the jury, but perhaps something else, coping with what they were hearing. Gans' book also provided a revelation. In 2004, Young's new defence team hired a forensic audiologist to analyse the six minute recording of the 999 call placed by Nicola Fuller. They determined that after Nicola was killed, footsteps of two different people could be heard rummaging around Blackman's Cottage, whispering to one another. While the whispers were unintelligible, one word was clear.
甘斯反驳了陪审员嘲弄富勒案并将酒店隔离视为派对的普遍看法。相反，他指出他们不得不坐着听令人不安的证据，包括尼古拉失败的999电话，这会让人感到难以置信的创伤。甘斯教授告诉澳大利亚广播公司：“那个酒店房间里发生的任何事情可能对陪审团来说都不是美好的时光，但也许是别的什么，是在应对他们所听到的事情。”甘斯的书还提供了一个启示。2004年，杨的新辩护团队聘请了一位法医听力学家来分析尼古拉·富勒拨打的999电话的六分钟录音。他们确定，在尼古拉被杀后，可以听到两个不同的人在布莱克曼小屋里翻找，互相耳语。虽然耳语听不清楚，但有一个词很清楚。

